] [17592186440816 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534843 17592186045417 true] [17592186440816 1071 "![](images/65/659db6f6f490b9ce311977713ffe52e96c04ebd2cb60ee95a0e241c455a6c6c7.png)\n\nWhat is the vertex of the parabola shown above?" 13194139534843 17592186045417 true] [17592186440816 1072 #uuid "2ec5d3c3-0881-5afc-b51d-bb796f5a2561" 13194139534843 17592186045417 true] [17592186440816 1074 "The vertex of an upward-opening parabola is the lowest point of the parabola.\n\n![](images/a0/a0e43112312f6fc14ec22d8fcefd13046c5f8be2fb980904b3f6a236a27dc9d2.png)\n\n  \n\nTherefore, the coordinates of the vertex are $(3,0).$" 13194139534843 17592186045417 true] [17592186440817 1068 #edb/ref 17592186440813 13194139534843 17592186045417 true] [17592186440817 1069 "q-85063" 13194139534843 17592186045417 true] [17592186440817 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139534843 17592186045417 true] [17592186440817 1071 "What are the coordinates of the vertex of the parabola $(y-3)^{2}=3(x-5)?$" 13194139534843 17592186045417 true] [17592186440817 1072 #uuid "8beb7550-388c-58d2-8337-e23626a88235" 13194139534843 17592186045417 true] [17592186440817 1074 "The standard equation of a left- or right-opening parabola that has its vertex at $(h,k)$ is\n\n$$\n(y-k)^{2}=4p(x-h),\n$$\n\nwhere $p$ is constant.\n\nWe can rewrite the given equation as \n\n$$\n(y-3)^{2}=4(\\frac{3}{4})(x-5).\n$$\n\nIt is now clear that our equation is of the standard type with $p=\\frac{3}{4}.$ \n\nComparing our equation with the standard equation, we can see that we have $h=5$ and $k=3.$ Therefore, the coordinates of the vertex of the parabola are $(5,3).$" 13194139534843 17592186045417 true] [17592186440818 1068 #edb/ref 17592186440814 13194139534843 17592186045417 true] [17592186440818 1069 "q-115894" 13194139534843 17592186045417 true] [17592186440818 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534843 17592186045417 true] [17592186440818 1071 "![](images/87/87f6b5b68c7447d154926023fae8f0215ea927d122f42e375b11d00e88a520e6.png)\n\nWhat is the vertex of the parabola shown above?" 13194139534843 17592186045417 true] [17592186440818 1072 #uuid "c70a41e9-d1c3-58ec-ac14-5fc542b5be6b" 13194139534843 17592186045417 true] [17592186440818 1074 "The vertex of a right-opening parabola is the left-most point of the parabola.\n\n![](images/b9/b9def5f9de72d5b739041cecf5d1cba3dd09a7c5fefc1001431b05f9820049b2.png)\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of the vertex are $(6,-2).$" 13194139534843 17592186045417 true] [17592186440819 1068 #edb/ref 17592186440815 13194139534843 17592186045417 true] [17592186440819 1069 "q-115909" 13194139534843 17592186045417 true] [17592186440819 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534843 17592186045417 true] [17592186440819 1071 "What are the coordinates of the vertex of the parabola ${y}^{2}=3x?$" 13194139534843 17592186045417 true] [17592186440819 1072 #uuid "eaf2fda4-efdd-5da9-b4eb-598434fc7b28" 13194139534843 17592186045417 true] [17592186440819 1074 "The standard equation of a left- or right-opening parabola that has its vertex at the origin is\n\n$$\n{y}^{2}=4px,\n$$\n\nwhere $p$ is a constant.\n\nWe can rewrite the given equation as \n\n$$\n{y}^{2}=4(\\frac{3}{4})x.\n$$\n\nIt is now clear that our equation is of the standard type with $p=\\frac{3}{4}.$ Therefore, our parabola has its vertex at $(0,0).$" 13194139534843 17592186045417 true]] :edb/tempids {"answer-08f5d885-41b3-5ff4-99ec-f4526e1acc1c" 17592186440783 "answer-0e158221-97dc-5854-80a8-edc02578c681" 17592186440784 "answer-0e4594bd-8770-5f77-89f6-e1306b377457" 17592186440785 "answer-147338d1-85cd-595c-a81f-5d0e46dc177f" 17592186440786 "answer-1cca29ea-a53e-5841-be71-7d086d2aa5d0" 17592186440787 "answer-336de5f5-e16f-54f1-8315-848c34ce189c" 17592186440788 "answer-48ae3ead-7c08-5f40-8fe0-d27c5273c8db" 17592186440789 "answer-54e965b8-c1a9-58ba-b962-2f2f97706924" 17592186440790 "answer-5f361fa5-ff06-5061-bd38-84c52a3c7b5f" 17592186440791 "answer-606fc074-de50-51a1-b962-f210edc955f2" 17592186440792 "answer-71eda